(2751874, 380003, 42808, '<td valign="top">No way! No way!-can''t believe it!! MY FIRST BLUE!! I screamed to myself when I saw the Blue Ribbon--#1. I am too thrilled and want to thank all of you for your inspiring votes and comments--It''s gonna be a good, NO GREAT day!!<br/> <br/>I was surprise at most of the comments who thought this was a real scene, especially with the guard-rope evidence near the bottom of shot,  but as a few of you acknowledged--it is actually a realistic sculpture in front of Contempory Art Institute of Chicago (title?). It is an actual car w/ trailer propped into the ground and lopsided!! Like anyone at first sight I thought it was an actual accident. It was mid afternoon, sat on steps in front of this sculpture and shot about 40 images of observing people surrounding it--waiting for the idea composition/story. Originally shot in color, I thought the bright yellow cab in background would be too distracting from the sculpture''s monotones. I''ve should have used a faster shutter (as suggested) and sharpened just a bit for better clarity-but rushed before the midnite deadline "Stupid Stupid"--could this qualify?  THANKS SO SO MUCH!!! -- Bus352<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-08-23 08:34:01.</i></td>', 'No way! No way!-can''t believe it!! MY FIRST BLUE!! I screamed to myself when I saw the Blue Ribbon--#1. I am too thrilled and want to thank all of you for your inspiring votes and comments--It''s gonna be a good, NO GREAT day!! I was surprise at most of the comments who thought this was a real scene, especially with the guard-rope evidence near the bottom of shot,  but as a few of you acknowledged--it is actually a realistic sculpture in front of Contempory Art Institute of Chicago (title?). It is an actual car w/ trailer propped into the ground and lopsided!! Like anyone at first sight I thought it was an actual accident. It was mid afternoon, sat on steps in front of this sculpture and shot about 40 images of observing people surrounding it--waiting for the idea composition/story. Originally shot in color, I thought the bright yellow cab in background would be too distracting from the sculpture''s monotones. I''ve should have used a faster shutter (as suggested) and sharpened just a bit for better clarity-but rushed before the midnite deadline "Stupid Stupid"--could this qualify?  THANKS SO SO MUCH!!! -- Bus352', '2006-08-23 09:15:24.000000', '2006-08-23 09:34:01.000000', 0),
(2751897, 378452, 48228, '<td valign="top">I agree with the other comments, as this is definately underrated and definately deserved to get a higher score. I also am pleased that you don''t smoke. I really like this one a lot Tim, and you are constantly giving us some excellent examples of photography..... Thank you very much.</td>', 'I agree with the other comments, as this is definately underrated and definately deserved to get a higher score. I also am pleased that you don''t smoke. I really like this one a lot Tim, and you are constantly giving us some excellent examples of photography..... Thank you very much.', '2006-08-23 09:22:39.000000', NULL, 0),
